  "details": "there's all these worlds in vrchat where you can watch things with friends supplied through youtube and discord, but there's some things you can't watch. Now obviously i'm not talking public listings, because these things aren't public, but what about capturing a window on your computer, and showing it on video players? E.g. I could put on an animation that's not on youtube, hosted on my own computer, in a browser or vlc, and show it to others in the world with me. \n\nof course this streaming would be something only vrc+ users could show, where everyone could watch who is in the instance, and nowhere else. \n\nit basically allows us to share any media we want with friends in vrchat for a nice chill and watch session",
